  "period_end": "2025-11-30",
  "title": "A larger model garden, one HTTP-shaped path",
  "summary": "November made Pollinations easier to build on: more models and media capabilities arrived while the routes from prompt to result became clearer, steadier, and more visible.\n\nClaude Sonnet 4.5, Grok 4 Fast, Kimi K2 Thinking, Gemini 3 Pro, Claude Opus 4.5, Perplexity Sonar, and Nano Banana Pro joined the API, alongside model discovery, cleaner aliases, real model IDs, and broader OpenAI-compatible request handling.\n\nImage infrastructure was simplified around enter.pollinations.ai, with better caching, retries, aspect-ratio preservation, reference-image support, clearer errors, 4K Nano Banana Pro output, and more reliable vision inputs.\n\nBuilders gained a Quick Start, browser-friendly CORS, direct text responses, streaming repairs, readable fallbacks, citations, usage tracking, cache invalidation, and audio support through OpenAI-compatible APIs. The machinery increasingly returns both answers and useful receipts.\n\nAuthentication, model routing, image caching, staging, and token handling converged around enter.pollinations.ai, while persistent Pollen accounting, balance refreshes, and clearer account status made usage plumbing more dependable.",
